<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Corvette Group off Bressay, 2022</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;This scenario assumes the United Kingdom has dramatically alters its relationship with the European Union and that&amp;nbsp;Europe suffers a major economic crisis around 2020.&amp;nbsp; Many Europeans blame the crisis on the U.K. and international tensions in Europe are at levels not seen since the end of the Cold War.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the last year alone, Norway and the United Kingdom have become embroiled in three separate disputes&amp;nbsp;over the use of the North Sea.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The situation has worsened&amp;nbsp;after a major storm in the North Sea results in the loss of several fishing boats, including a number of Norwegian vessels.&amp;nbsp; Norway has blamed the United Kingdom for not doing more to help rescue the crews of these vessels.&amp;nbsp; This tragic situation has turned dangerous due to the inflamatory remarks made a few days&amp;nbsp;after the storm&amp;nbsp;on a British radio broadcast.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The United Kingdom suspects that a Norweigan surface action group is headed for the Shetland Islands.&amp;nbsp; Its intentions appear to&amp;nbsp;be to&amp;nbsp;conduct&amp;nbsp;some kind of punitive strike;&amp;nbsp;the radio station on&amp;nbsp;Bressay, from which the anti-Norwegian&amp;nbsp;remarks were broadcast, is&amp;nbsp;a very likely target.&amp;nbsp; Although a raid of this nature does not represent a serious threat to the United Kingdom, it does constitute a serious threat to the lives and property of the people living on Bressay, and the&amp;nbsp;British government&amp;nbsp;has no intention of allowing it to take place.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
